{
  "_schema": "KJV → Hebrew (OSHB/WLC) versification map. For each KJV OT verse, computes the Hebrew verse_id(s) it should attach to. Two layers: (a) `psalms_offsets` — chapter→offset for Psalms; (b) `book_overrides` — per-book per-range overrides for chapter-boundary shifts. KJV verses without a matching override fall through to direct (KJV.ch.v → Heb.ch.v). An override may carry `extra_targets` to encode merge cases (one KJV verse covers multiple Heb verses, or vice versa).",
  "_source_notes": "All offsets and overrides verified against OSHB chapter sizes and the KJV scrollmapper text. Boundary-verse content was checked verse-by-verse via _probe_oshb_verses scripts before encoding. Where one KJV verse covers two Heb verses (NUM 26:1 = Heb 25:19+26:1; 1SA 20:42 = Heb 20:42+21:1; 1CH 12:4 = Heb 12:4+5; 1KI 22:43 = Heb 22:43+44; ISA 64:1 = Heb 63:19+64:1) we list the secondary Heb verse under `extra_targets`. Where two KJV verses collapse into one Heb verse (NEH 7:67-68 = Heb 7:67), the ingest concatenates the two KJV texts at the same Heb target.",
  "_phase": "Phase 2C-7 — full KJV OT versification (closes the 6-skipped-books gap and the 66 chapter-boundary gap verses from Phase 2C-6).",
